  "title": "Medicine for Dyspnoea (Difficulty in Breathing)",
  "data": "According to a narration, al-Mufaddal complained to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) of dyspnoea (difficulty in breathing, or shortness of breath), saying, “Whenever I walk, I find it hard to breathe, and I have to sit down to rest.” Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) told him, “Drink camels' urine, and this disease will be calmed.”\nAccording to another tradition, a man complained to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) of a cough, and the Imam (a.s.) directed him to a remedy, saying, “Put an amount of lovage (a medicinal herb) and a similar amount of sugar in the palm of your hand and swallow the mixture, for one or two days.” The man said, “I needed to do this only once, and I was healed.”"
}
